  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nDuring the [firing of a successful download request navigate event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fire-a-download-request-navigate-event), the `navigation`'s [ongoing navigate event](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#ongoing-navigate-event) is set. However, the ongoing navigate event is only later cleared in either the case of an [aborted navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#ongoing-navigation-tracking:ongoing-navigate-event-2) or a [same-document navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate-event-firing:ongoing-navigate-event-4), which [download requests are not](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#fire-a-download-request-navigate-event:~:text=Set%20destination%27s%20is%20same%20document%20to%20false). This means that if two successful download request navigate events are fired in a row, the [`navigation's ongoing navigate event is null` assertion](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigate-event-firing:ongoing-navigate-event) will fail.\n\nThis case does not seem to have been covered by https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11579.\n\nThis was discovered during the investigation of an issue reported in Firefox: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1994531\n\ncc @noamr",
